# User-declared Equatable instance for Point type — cross-dict dispatch.
#
# Parent dispatch chaining: dict 3's = MethodDispatcher (no Point arm) now forwards to
# dict 2's = MethodDispatcher via a captured parent-scope reference. This fixes the
# cross-dict chaining gap.
#
# User-defined nominal type dispatch: when a VarRef pin pattern resolves to a
# type-constructor Dict and the scrutinee is a Variant, match_pattern compares the
# Variant's tycon field against the pattern name. The Point arm now matches correctly, and
# the custom Equatable instance fires. p1 = p2 → Boolean.True (same x, y), p1 = p3 →
# Boolean.False (different y).
[Point: [type Point: [x: Int y: Int]]]
[instance Equatable
  [let a@Point]: [=: [fn [let p q]
    [and [= p.x q.x] [= p.y q.y]]]]]
[
  p1: [Point.Point x: 1 y: 2]
  p2: [Point.Point x: 1 y: 2]
  p3: [Point.Point x: 1 y: 3]
  # Point arm matches via user-type dispatch — custom equality fires.
  same: [= p1 p2]
  diff: [= p1 p3]
]
=== out
Dict({"p1": Variant(Point.Point, Dict({"x": Int(1), "y": Int(2)})), "p2": Variant(Point.Point, Dict({"x": Int(1), "y": Int(2)})), "p3": Variant(Point.Point, Dict({"x": Int(1), "y": Int(3)})), "same": Variant(Boolean.True, Null), "diff": Variant(Boolean.False, Null)})
